  "question_stem": "A runner sets off from a point $P$ at time $t = 0$, where $t$ is in seconds. The runner starts from rest and accelerates at $1.2 \\text{ m s}^{-2}$ for $5 \\text{ s}$. For the next $12 \\text{ s}$ the runner moves at constant speed before decelerating uniformly over a period of $3 \\text{ s}$, coming to rest at $Q$. A cyclist sets off from $P$ at time $t = 10$ and accelerates uniformly for $10 \\text{ s}$, before immediately decelerating uniformly to rest at $Q$ at time $t = 30$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "Runner graph has vertices $(0,0),(5,6),(17,6),(20,0)$; $PQ=96$ m."
